s":"drum"}],"gloss":"drum","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தெண்கண்","parts":[{"text":"தெண்கண்","lemma":"தெண்கண்","gloss":"clear drumhead"}],"gloss":"clear drumhead","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தெளிர்ப்ப","parts":[{"text":"தெளிர்ப்ப","lemma":"தெளிர்த்தல்","gloss":"to sound clearly"}],"gloss":"to sound clearly"},{"surface":"வொற்றிப்","parts":[{"text":"வொற்றிப்","lemma":"வொற்றிப்","gloss":"beating"}],"gloss":"beating","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடி","parts":[{"text":"பாடி","lemma":"பாடுதல்","gloss":"having sung"}],"gloss":"having sung"},{"surface":"வந்தது","parts":[{"text":"வந்தது","lemma":"வருதல்","gloss":"that which came"}],"gloss":"that which came"},{"surface":"எல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லாம்","lemma":"எல்லாம்","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"all"},{"surface":"கோடியர்","parts":[{"text":"கோடியர்","lemma":"கோடியர்","gloss":"bards"}],"gloss":"bards"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முழவுமருள்","parts":[{"text":"முழவு","lemma":"முழவு","gloss":"drum"},{"text":"மருள்","lemma":"மருள்","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"resembling a drum"},{"surface":"திருமணி","parts":[{"text":"திரு","lemma":"திரு","gloss":"beautiful"},{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"gem"}],"gloss":"beautiful gems"},{"surface":"மிடைந்தநின்","parts":[{"text":"மிடைந்த","lemma":"மிடைதல்","gloss":"crowded"},{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"crowded on your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அரவுறழ்","parts":[{"text":"அரவு","lemma":"அரவு","gloss":"serpent"},{"text":"உறழ்","lemma":"உறழ்","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"resembling a serpent"},{"surface":"ஆரம்","parts":[{"text":"ஆரம்","lemma":"ஆரம்","gloss":"necklace"}],"gloss":"necklace"},{"surface":"முகக்குவம்","parts":[{"text":"முக","lemma":"முகத்தல்","gloss":"gather"},{"text":"குவம்","lemma":"குவம்","gloss":"we will"}],"gloss":"we will gather"},{"surface":"எனவே","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"saying so"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"saying so indeed"}]}],"literal":"If we say we will gather and return with elephants, / Like hills that ward off the shining rain clouds, / All the elephants have perished, hit by arrows. / If we say we will gather tall chariots with lotus-seats, / The good horses of fast gallop collapsed when pulled back, / Their great pride destroyed, they reached the ground. / If we say we will gather horses with trimmed manes, / With bodies filled with scars, they met their great death, / Like ships whose course is cut off by the wind, / They abounded in a great flood of blood. There, / Because there is nothing to receive, without joy, / Suppliants grieve in this painful, wide battlefield. / O plowman who uses the sword as a plow to destroy men! / Beating my drum, whose clear drumhead is like the footprint of a rutting elephant, / So that it sounds clearly, / All the bards who came singing, / Resembling a drum, interspersed with beautiful gems, on your / Serpent-like necklace, saying 'we will gather' indeed!","translation":"If we think of gathering elephants and returning, they lie dead, hit by arrows, looking like hills that once blocked the rain clouds. If we think of taking tall chariots with lotus-shaped seats, their swift horses have collapsed, their pride ruined, fallen to the ground. If we think of taking horses with trimmed manes, they have met their death, covered in wounds, floating in a vast flood of blood like ships wrecked when the wind fails. In this painful, wide battlefield where suppliants grieve with nothing to take, O warrior who plows with a sword to destroy enemies! I beat my clear-skinned drum, which is as wide as the footprint of a rutting elephant, making it sound loud. All of us bards have come singing, hoping only to receive the serpent-like necklace of beautiful, drum-sized gems that adorns your chest!","modern":"யானைகளைக் கவர்ந்து செல்லலாம் என்று நினைத்தால், அவை மேகங்களைத் தடுக்கும் மலைகளைப் போல அம்புகள் பட்டு மடிந்து கிடக்கின்றன. தாமரை மொட்டு போன்ற கொடுஞ்சியைக் கொண்ட பெரிய தேர்களைக் கவர்ந்து செல்லலாம் என்று நினைத்தால், அவற்றின் வேகமான குதிரைகள் இழுக்கப்படும்போது சரிந்து, பெருமை அழிந்து தரையில் வீழ்ந்து கிடக்கின்றன. கத்தரித்த பிடரிமயிரைக் கொண்ட குதிரைகளைக் கவர்ந்து செல்லலாம் என்று நினைத்தால், அவை உடம்பெல்லாம் காயங்களுடன் இறந்து, காற்று இல்லாததால் நடுக்கடலில் நின்ற கப்பல்களைப் போல, குருதி வெள்ளத்தில் மிதக்கின்றன. இவ்வாறு பரிசில் பெறுவதற்கு ஏதும் இல்லாததால், இரப்பவர்கள் வருந்தும் இந்தத் துன்பம் நிறைந்த போர்க்களத்தில், வாளையே ஏராகக் கொண்டு பகைவர்களை அழித்த உழவனே! மதயானையின் காலடி போன்ற எனது தெடாரிப் பறையின் தெளிந்த கண்ணைத் தட்டி ஒலிக்கச் செய்து, பாடி வந்த பாணர்கள் அனைவரும், உன்னுடைய மார்பில் விளங்கும், முழவு போன்ற பெரிய மணிகள் கோத்த, பாம்பு போன்ற ஆரத்தைப் பெற்றுக் கொள்வோம் என்றே வந்துள்ளோம்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Kaḻāttalaiyār addresses the Cēra king Kuṭakkō Neṭuñcēralātaṉ on a vast, blood-soaked battlefield. The poet describes how the usual spoils of war, such as elephants, horses, and chariots, have all been completely destroyed in the fierce combat. The elephants lie like fallen hills, the horses have perished with deep wounds, and the chariots are broken on the ground. Because there are no intact spoils left to be given as gifts, the bards and suppliants are left grieving on this painful field. Therefore, the poet beats his drum and declares that the bards have come singing only to receive the beautiful, serpent-like gem necklace worn by the victorious king himself.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}